Handling commands
In the previous section, we created a simple web API and learned that the API is the edge of
our application. The edge talks with the outside world and accepts requests via HTTP or
another communication protocol. To execute these requests, we need an application service
that works as an intermediary between edge components and the domain model. The
application service is also responsible for persisting entities.
